  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f57" contextRef="c1">&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;times new roman&#39;, &#39;serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-top: 0;text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;times new roman&#39;, &#39;serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;SPIRE NGL INC.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;times new roman&#39;, &#39;serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-top: 0;text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;times new roman&#39;, &#39;serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;NOTES TO FINANCIAL STATEMENTS&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;times new roman&#39;, &#39;serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-top: 0;text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;times new roman&#39;, &#39;serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-style:italic;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;For the Three and Twelve Months Ended December 31, 2025 and 2024&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.3pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 0.05pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div  style="color: #000000;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.3pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 0.05pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div  style="color: #000000;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.3pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 0.05pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Note I - Summary of Accounting Policies&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-right: 0.35in;margin-top: 0;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;letter-spacing: -0.1pt;;display:inline;"&gt;Spire NGL Inc. (the Company or Spire NGL), was incorporated in Missouri on April 17, 1962 and is 100% owned by Spire Resources LLC. The Company owns and operates a 40-mile pipeline between Missouri and Illinois.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 17.25pt;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-right: 0.25in;margin-top: 11.9pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Regulation: Spire NGL is regulated by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) which establishes rates for the interstate transmission of natural gas and oil. Regulation is intended to permit the recovery, through rates, of the cost of service including a rate of return on the investment.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.3pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-right: 0.25in;margin-top: 0;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;The financial statements of Spire NGL are prepared in accordance with accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, or FERC USA, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America, or GAAP.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-right: 0.25in;margin-top: 11.5pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;The more significant differences between accounting principles generally accepted in the United States (GAAP) and those promulgated by FERC are:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 11.5pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;Account Classification: The classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet and statement of income. Allowance for Funds Used During Construction (AFUDC): AFUDC represents the cost of capital during the construction period of plant and equipment. The calculation consists of debt and equity portions in accordance with FERC guidelines. Interest capitalized for GAAP does not contain an equity portion.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-right: 0.35in;margin-top: 11.55pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Use of Estimates: The preparation of financial statements in conformity with accounting principles generally accepted in the United States and the accounting requirements of the FERC requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the amounts of assets and liabilities and disclosure of contingent liabilities reported in the financial statements and accompanying notes. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-right: 0.55in;margin-top: 11.35pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div  style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;letter-spacing: -0.15pt;;display:inline;"&gt;Revenue Recognition: Revenues are recognized in the period that services are provided or products delivered. Spire NGL may periodically collect revenues subject to possible refunds pending final orders from the FERC. When such situations arise, the &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;Company establishes reserves for revenues collected subject to refund.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-right: 0.45in;margin-top: 11.5pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;Property, Plant and Equipment: Property, plant and equipment are stated at cost. The cost of property, plant and equipment are depreciated in the financial statements using the straight-line method.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 11.8pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Note 2 - Rate Matters, Litigation&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 20.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 0;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;There is no pending or threatened litigation.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 5.85pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Note 3 - Related-Party Transactions&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 5.85pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div  style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;Spire NGL loaned money to affiliates and received related interest income. The Company also &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;participated in normal intercompany shared services transactions.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 12.35pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Note 4 - Employee Benefits&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 0;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div  style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;Spire NGL has no employees and therefore incurred no direct pension costs and has no pension plan. It does have indirect pension costs from the work performed for it by affiliated companies. &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 11.95pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Note 5 &amp;#8211; Cash Flow Statements&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.40in;margin-top: 11.95pt;text-indent: -0.25in;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;A)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="spacecount: 4;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;For the three and nine months ended September 30, 2025 and 2024, Spire NGL made $0 in cash income tax payments, respectively.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.40in;margin-top: 11.95pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div  style="color: #000000;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 11.95pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Note 6 &amp;#8211; Income Taxes&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 0;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div  style="color: #000000;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 0;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;The Company&amp;#8217;s accounting for income taxes is impacted by ASC 980, Regulated Operations. Reductions in deferred income tax balances due to the reduction in the corporate income tax rate will result in amounts previously collected from customers for these deferred taxes to be refundable to such customers, generally through reductions in future rates. The Tax Cuts and Jobs Act that went into effect January 1, 2018 included provisions that stipulate how these excess deferred taxes are to be passed back to customers for certain accelerated tax depreciation benefits. The treatment for accumulated deferred income tax balances for Spire NGL is yet to be determined by FERC.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div  style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 0;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div  style="color: #000000;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 0;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;&lt;div style="font-weight:bold;display:inline;"&gt;Note 7 - Subsequent Events&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;line-height: 11.4pt;margin-bottom: 19.2pt;margin-left: 0.15in;margin-top: 0.55pt;vertical-align: baseline;"&gt;&lt;div style="color: #000000;font-family: &#39;arial&#39;, &#39;sans-serif&#39;;font-size: 10pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;letter-spacing: -0.05pt;;display:inline;"&gt;Subsequent events have been evaluated through the date that the financial statements were issued on April 15, 2026. On January 1, 2026, Spire Inc. completed the sale of Spire NGL Inc. to Phillips 66.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="font-family: &#39;times new roman&#39;, &#39;serif&#39;;font-size: 11pt;margin-bottom: 0;margin-top: 0;"&gt;&lt;div  style="font-size: 11pt;font-style: ;font-weight: ;;display:inline;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
